# Cloudflare Pages routing for wearthemood.com
#
# On the DigitalOcean droplet, Caddy reverse-proxies /r/* to the API container
# (deploy/Caddyfile: `handle /r/* { reverse_proxy api:8000 }`). Cloudflare Pages
# serves static assets only, so without this rule every referral link would 404
# the moment the apex is pointed at Pages — silently breaking install attribution
# (§24) for every share already in the wild.
#
# Pages `_redirects` cannot transparently proxy to another origin, so this is a
# 302 to the API, which records the attribution and then issues its own redirect.
# One extra hop versus Caddy's reverse-proxy; the referral code is preserved.
/r/*    https://api.wearthemood.com/r/:splat    302

# Admin console. THIS is the rule the note below used to say was still missing —
# and its absence is exactly why the console stopped opening. Caddy used to proxy
# /mood-ops-console-7x9* to the admin-web container; after the apex moved to
# Pages (2026-08-03) nothing served that path at all, so it fell through to the
# Pages 404. The admin app itself was healthy on Heroku the whole time.
#
# Pages cannot transparently proxy to another origin, so this is a 302 to the
# Heroku admin host — the same shape as /r/* above. The base path is preserved
# because the Next app is built with `basePath=/mood-ops-console-7x9` and 404s
# without it. Two rules: the bare path (no trailing slash) and everything under
# it; `_redirects` does not match the parent from a /* rule alone.
#
# No security change: the Heroku host is already publicly reachable, auth is
# unchanged, and the IP allowlist (when set) reads x-forwarded-for, which Heroku
# populates with the real client IP just as Cloudflare did.
#
# A Cloudflare Origin Rule would keep the wearthemood.com URL instead of
# redirecting, which is the nicer end state — it needs a zone-scoped API token
# (the token in use is Pages-scoped) so it is not something this file can do.
/mood-ops-console-7x9      https://wtm-admin-aab1ebe5235d.herokuapp.com/mood-ops-console-7x9/login    302
/mood-ops-console-7x9/*    https://wtm-admin-aab1ebe5235d.herokuapp.com/mood-ops-console-7x9/:splat   302
#
# Legal pages: Pages serves the canonical extensionless URLs (/legal/privacy etc.)
# and 308s the .html forms to them. Published/store-listing URLs should use the
# extensionless form after cutover.
